OL,3,ATrump ordered to answer questions under
OL,4,Aoath in BBC lawsuit
OL,5,
OL,6,FA US judge has ordered President Donald
OL,7,FTrump to answer questions under oath in
OL,8,Fhis defamation lawsuit against the BBC
OL,9,Fby 11 December.
OL,11,FTrump is suing the BBC over an episode
OL,12,Fof Panorama that edited together two
OL,13,Fdifferent sections of a speech he gave
OL,14,Fbefore the riot at the US Capitol in
OL,15,F2021.
OL,23,APub: 22-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,0,100
PN,11908
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F119A1792707514
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs15j 5ws
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,ATrump ordered to answer questions under
OL,4,Aoath in BBC lawsuit
OL,5,
OL,6,FCharles Tobin, a lawyer representing
OL,7,Fthe BBC, said in court that "we still
OL,8,Fhaven't been able to depose the
OL,9,Fplaintiff" with two months left in the
OL,10,Fdiscovery period, during which both
OL,11,Fsides are legally required to exchange
OL,12,Finformation with each other on their
OL,13,Fcase.
OL,15,FTrump cancelled a previous deposition
OL,16,Fon 16 October, citing "matters of
OL,17,Fnational importance" while he was
OL,18,Fcampaigning in Georgia.
OL,23,APub: 22-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG8/39
